--panel, rgba(20,20,24,0.9));\n}","patch_id":"p10","time":1793905359031},{"author":"agent","facet":"js","label":"R2.7: the status no longer paints outside the slot — drop the stale sentence","new":"// R2.6: every string here is peer-reported (msg, err, the peer name) —\n// textContent only, one div per line so the err text and the update\n// sentence read apart.","old":"// R2.6: every string here is peer-reported (msg, err, the peer name) —\n// textContent only, one div per line so the err text and the update\n// sentence read apart. The status paints under the tile's fixed box.","patch_id":"p11","time":1793905362137},{"author":"promote","cmd":"","facet":"memory","label":"promote: fold -> peer.reboot","new":"[\n{\"claim\": \"The peer.reboot dashboard tile draws a fixed 150x150 canvas but its status line (.rebootstatus) sits in normal flow BELOW the canvas, so a long message grows the tile and pushes the rows below it down instead of painting over a neighbour.\", \"detail\": \"R2.7 (2026-11-05). The icon slot in peer.headsup css (D4) is min-height:150px, not a fixed height, so the tile grows with its status. peer.reboot's redraw() sizes the canvas square from the slot WIDTH (h = w), never clientHeight, so the drawing stays 150x150 however tall the status gets. The status is textContent-only, one div per line. Verified in the rig at 1440x900, panel 360px, and with the tiles reordered Reboot->Camera: the ~374-char Linux failure sentence grew the reboot tile to 412px and the camera tile moved down a clean 12px gap with no overlap.\", \"tags\": \"peer,reboot,ui,dashboard,layout,R2.7\", \"source\": {\"lib\": \"peer\", \"ctl\": \"reboot\", \"facet\": \"css\", \"hash\": \"f9d4f8149276162a\"}, \"confidence\": \"high\", \"time\": 1793907057123},\n{\"end\": true}]\n","old":"","patch_id":"p12","time":1793907059405}]},"id":"ygmyio1842ea11cb6oa_patches","readers":[],"time":1793907059405,"username":"system","writers":[]}